### Texture generation

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `data/Assets/Tools/generate_seasonal_textures.py` | One-time offline script (git-tracked): extracts texture from USDZ, generates spring + fall + winter variants |
| `data/Assets/SeasonalTextures/` | Output directory for generated PNGs (gitignored via `*.png`, `.gitkeep` tracked) |

The output directory deliberately lives outside the Nucleus sync tree (`data/nucleus/`). This means a `pullnucleus.bat` run — even a full clean + re-pull — will never destroy the generated textures. The source USDZ is still read from `data/nucleus/` (where it belongs as Nucleus-synced content).

**Setup for new developers**: run `preinstall.bat` (pulls Nucleus content + generates textures automatically). Alternatively, run `pullnucleus.bat` and `runscripts.bat` separately. To regenerate textures only: `runscripts.bat`. Requires `Pillow` and `numpy` (`pip install -r kit-app-template-main/source/data/Assets/Tools/requirements.txt`).

#### Texture generation details

The script extracts the 4096×4096 RGBA atlas from the USDZ and processes only the **right half** (x ≥ 2048 — the leaf sprites). The left half (bark/trunk) is always kept untouched.

| Variant | Technique |
|---------|-----------|
| **Spring** | Block-grid removal: divide leaf region into 64×64 px blocks; randomly remove 25 % of blocks (zero RGBA). Keeps original green colour. Different random seed from fall so the gap pattern differs. |
| **Fall** | Block-grid removal + colour mix: each 64×64 block is randomly assigned a role — remove (25 %), stay green (7.5 %), turn orange (7.5 %), or turn golden yellow (60 %). Transparent pixels have RGB zeroed to prevent mipmap bleed. |
| **Winter** | All RGBA channels zeroed on the right half. Leaf geometry becomes invisible via alpha cutout. |

Key constants in the script:

| Constant | Value | Purpose |
|----------|-------|---------|
| `SPLIT_X` | 2048 | Left/right boundary in the atlas |
| `BLOCK_SIZE` | 64 | Spatial grid block size (px) |
| `FALL_LEAF_REMOVE_FRACTION` | 0.25 | Fraction of leaf blocks removed |
| `FALL_COLOR_YELLOW` | 0.80 | Dominant autumn colour |
| `FALL_COLOR_GREEN` | 0.10 | Untouched green blocks |
| `FALL_COLOR_ORANGE` | 0.10 | Deep orange blocks |

**Mipmap bleed prevention**: transparent pixels must have all four channels (RGBA) set to zero, not just alpha. Otherwise, at distance the GPU averages coloured-but-transparent texels into visible mip levels, causing "ghost" green hazes around winter/fall trees.

**Missing textures fallback**: if the generated PNGs are absent (script not yet run), the extension logs `[seasons] texture missing for '<season>' — keeping current appearance`, dispatches both `seasonChangeStarted` and `seasonChangeCompleted` (so the view transition overlay fades back in immediately), and returns without modifying any shaders. Trees remain in their current appearance — no crash, no stuck overlay.

